{"t": 1794107274.973377, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "files": [{"content": "def deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the standard headers for a deprecated endpoint.\n\n    ``sunset_date`` is the HTTP-date the caller supplies and is sent as-is.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "path": "api/headers.py"}], "message": "ENG-91: add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794107277.0870056, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` per ENG-91 and the Deprecation section of the API guidelines (Notion).\n\nDeprecated endpoints now return:\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` (the sunset date passed in, unchanged)\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nCloses ENG-91.", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints"}, "ok": true}
